# Test: a SIGHUP reload moves the web, looking-glass and MCP listeners
# VALIDATES: a reload whose config changes the listen port of the web server,
#   the looking glass and the MCP server moves each listener without a restart:
#   the new port answers, the old port refuses new connections, and a connection
#   accepted on the old port before the reload still answers after it.
# PREVENTS: a listen-address change that needs a daemon restart, or one that
#   leaves the old port open, or one that cuts the connections it had accepted.
#
# The fixture (internal/test/fixture/listener_migration_fixture.go) starts the
# daemon itself, on six free ports it picks, because the runner leases two and
# the scenario needs a before and an after port for each of three services. It
# returns an error, reported through ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL, at the first service whose
# migration does not hold.
option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/listener-migration:timeout=90s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: web moved from port
expect=stdout:contains=OK: looking-glass moved from port
expect=stdout:contains=OK: mcp moved from port
